  "name": "VancouFur",
  "shortName": "VF",
  "description": "VancouFur is a furry convention, held over four days since 2014, in the Vancouver area of British Columbia, run by volunteers and the British Columbia Anthropomorphic Events Association. It was first held in March 2012 at the Executive Hotel and Conference Centre in Burnaby, with 347 attendees. It moved to Richmond in 2016, spent 2020 and 2022 to 2024 at the Sheraton Vancouver Guildford in Surrey, and returned to the Richmond conference centre near the airport in 2025. Attendance reached 3,069 in 2026. Since 2021 its charity partner has been QMUNITY, which received C$20,000 from the convention in both 2023 and 2024.",
